# Send the Netlify subdomain to the custom domain. Netlify does not do this on
# its own - a primary custom domain only adds a rel="canonical" header, which
# search engines may honour and a person following an old link never will.
# Full URLs on the left: a bare /* would match the custom domain too and
# redirect it to itself forever. The ! forces the rule over index.html.
# 302 while this is new; switch to 301 once it has run a while, since browsers
# cache a 301 almost permanently.
https://usajobs-tracker.netlify.app/*  https://usajobs-tracker.abigailhaddad.com/:splat  302!
http://usajobs-tracker.netlify.app/*   https://usajobs-tracker.abigailhaddad.com/:splat  302!
